WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.870
Helpsters, our goal is to hand out

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.000
a frozen freeze pops to cool down the neighborhood.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.490
Now who's got an idea?

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:09.990
[INAUDIBLE]

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:10.500
Yeah?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.470
We want the neighborhood to know we have freeze pops,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.720
so we should tell the neighborhood

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.810
we have freeze pops.

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:18.630
But what if you cannot hear us?

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.540
You know, mother Primm always says

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.210
to speak softly and carry a big megaphone.

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:25.710
[DING]

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.810
Use a megaphone to make our voices louder.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.480
If we are going to give out freeze pops,

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.630
we need freeze pops, right?

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:34.980
Yeah, we do.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.390
And that's job two, make freeze pops.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:37.890
[DING]

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.530
So how do we stop the freeze pops from melting

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.480
before we hand them out?

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.900
That is job three.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:44.400
[DING]

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.890
Find a way to keep the freeze pops cold.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.890
I shall find a megaphone to make our voices louder.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:50.550
Hm.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.790
I'll make the freeze pops.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.630
And I will find a way to keep them cold.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.350
Fantastic.

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.320
Well, looks like everything's going great.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.390
Nothing's going great.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.620
What do you mean, Mr. Primm?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.170
I went to the megaphone room to get a megaphone,

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.300
but when I got there, it was empty except for this.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.895
Oh, huh, no megaphones.

00:01:10.895 --> 00:01:11.900
Mm-hm.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:12.590
No problem.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.480
We'll just make a new megaphone.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:15.680
With what?

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.930
Well, with the paper in your hand, you know, the sign.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:18.430
Hm?

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.150
Just follow my commands, OK?

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:20.750
OK.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.696
First, roll the paper into a cone.

00:01:23.696 --> 00:01:24.815
All right?

00:01:24.815 --> 00:01:26.680
OK, and next, tape the edges together.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:27.180
All right.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.030
Just use that tape the megaphones use

00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:30.540
to hang up the sign, right?

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.580
What a lovely idea, yes.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.080
Great, all right, looks good.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.450
And last, hold the small end in your mouth and talk.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.430
Testing!

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.100
My voice is louder.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:43.850
It is.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.656
Use a megaphone to make our voices louder, check.

00:01:46.656 --> 00:01:47.156
[DING]

00:01:47.156 --> 00:01:48.720
Um, Cody?

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.220
Yeah.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.140
I need your help in the kitchen.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:53.250
OK, right behind you.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.160
So talk to me, buddy-bud.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.220
Every time I try to make them, it doesn't work.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.090
Oh, why don't you show me your sequence.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.050
OK.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:02.830
First, pour the juice into the tray.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:11.210
OK, looking good.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.127
Next, add the stick.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:20.568
Hm, look at that, just falls right over.

00:02:20.568 --> 00:02:22.610
Yeah, but in the picture, they stand straight up.

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:26.330
Right, well, looks like we've got to debug.

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.160
That means find and fix the problem, right?

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:28.730
Yeah.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:32.750
So the sticks keep falling over in the juice, huh?

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.830
Well, we need something to hold them up.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:35.390
But what?

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.390
Oh, hey, you have any plastic wrap?

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:39.560
Always.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:43.775
OK, then, new sequence, first, pour the juice into the trays.

00:02:43.775 --> 00:02:45.250
I already did that.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.220
Yeah, you did.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:48.705
Next, cover the tray with plastic wrap.

00:02:48.705 --> 00:02:49.205
Covering.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:55.244
Mm-hm, next, add the sticks.

00:02:55.244 --> 00:02:55.744
Hm.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:00.710
The plastic makes the sticks stand up.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.700
Yeah, look at that.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:04.185
Now add the rest of the sticks, buddy bud.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.140
Na-na!

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:08.660
Mm-hm.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.510
OK, then, put the tray in the freezer.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.760
OK.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.260
Got this.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.630
Mm-hm, don't spill. don't spill.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:15.770
You got this.

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:16.070
Don't spill.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:16.350
You got this.

